NUM-03: put the parenthesis of the RECT_ROUND round-bottom hydraulic radius in the right place

XsectEval::rect_round_getRofY() returned 0.5*r*(1 - sin(t))/t for a depth inside the
circular bottom. The hydraulic radius of a circular segment is
A/P = 0.5*r*(1 - sin(t)/t), which rect_round_getRofA() already uses. Dynamic
wave takes its friction slope from this function, so in RECT_ROUND conduits
flowing inside the round bottom the hydraulic radius was too large near the
invert, zero at y = 0.29r and up to 100x too small above that.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-03_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydraulics/XSectKernels.hpp b/src/engine/hydraulics/XSectKernels.hpp
index 0b24251..6eac01a 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydraulics/XSectKernels.hpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydraulics/XSectKernels.hpp
@@ -785,7 +785,7 @@ struct XsectEval {
         if (y <= 0.0) return 0.0;
         if (y > xs.y_bot) return rect_round_getRofA(xs, rect_round_getAofY(xs, y));
         double theta1 = 2.0 * std::acos(1.0 - y / xs.r_bot);
-        return 0.5 * xs.r_bot * (1.0 - std::sin(theta1)) / theta1;
+        return 0.5 * xs.r_bot * (1.0 - std::sin(theta1) / theta1);
     }
 
     OPENSWMM_KERNEL_FN double rect_round_getSofA(const XSectParams& xs, double a) const {
